    misreading: "Do not read “throw dust in their faces” as a call to be rude to people who are kind to you. Ghazali explains it as showing that you dislike praise. The righteous in the section answer with prayers and humility.",
    sourceAnchor: "Book 24, Bane 18 concluded: what the one praised must do. Arabic pages 907 in the Shamela edition.",
    model: { kind: "chain", title: "Hearing praise", items: [{ label: "Remember what you know", body: "Your hidden thoughts, faults and uncertain end.", role: "support" }, { label: "Dislike the praise", body: "Show it, as the righteous did.", role: "support" }, { label: "Turn it into a prayer", body: "Forgive me what they do not know; make me better than they think.", role: "support" }], caption: "What the one praised should do." },
